```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class StockPriceManipulator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.println("Welcome to the Stock Price Manipulator!");
        System.out.println("Please enter the current stock price:");
        double currentPrice = scanner.nextDouble();

        System.out.println("Please enter the desired stock price:");
        double desiredPrice = scanner.nextDouble();

        System.out.println("Please enter the number of shares you wish to buy:");
        int numShares = scanner.nextInt();

        double profit = calculateProfit(currentPrice, desiredPrice, numShares);
        System.out.println("Your potential profit is: $" + profit);
    }

    public static double calculateProfit(double currentPrice, double desiredPrice, int numShares) {
        double difference = desiredPrice - currentPrice;
        double quantity = numShares * difference;
        return quantity;
    }
}
```

This code prompts the user to input the current stock price, desired stock price, and number of shares they wish to buy. It then calculates the potential profit based on the difference between the desired and current prices and the number of shares purchased. The profit is printed to the console.

